{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 34, :comments ["<b>Do not fear him.</b> Rashi explained that Moses was afraid to do battle, lest Og's merit stand for him, etc. And if you ask: why was Moses our master afraid? Behold, in the portion of לך לך, Rashi himself explained that Og intended that Abraham be killed so that he might take Sarah his wife — one may answer, even so, it is a merit for him, as we say in tractate Horayot, chapter כהן משיח: Rav Yehuda said in the name of Rav: a person should always engage in Torah and commandments even שלא לשמה (not for their own sake), for through the merit of forty-two offerings that Balak king of Moab brought, he merited and Ruth daughter of Eglon emerged from him, as Rabbi Yosi said: Ruth daughter of Eglon, grandson of Balak king of Moab, she was. And therefore too Moses our master was afraid lest the merit stand for him, that he told Abraham the Hebrew that his brother was taken captive — until HaShem said to him: <b>do not fear him.</b>"], :book :numbers, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:19:13.272662895Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}